> 参考译文：
Chinese paper-cutting is a traditional folk art with a history of more than 2,000 years. Paper-cutting requires simple materials, mainly red paper. During festivals,
people cut patterns of flowers, birds and figures to express good wishes. Passed down from generation to generation, this art is deeply loved by people both at home and abroad.
